{{!-- A2, "title page + rail": no cover photo, the titling carries the page, and the contents
list and share actions ride along in a sticky rail.

`items-start` is what makes the rail sticky at all. Grid items stretch by default, so the aside
would be as tall as the article and `position: sticky` on a full-height box has nothing to
scroll within. The rail's own `max-stack:static` and this grid's `max-stack:grid-cols-…` are the
same decision at the same token: below `stack` there is one column, so nothing may stick. --}}
{{> "post/title-page"}}

<div class="container pt-14">
	<div
		class="max-stack:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] max-stack:gap-10 grid grid-cols-[232px_minmax(0,1fr)] items-start gap-[72px]">
		{{> "post/rail"}}

		<div class="measure min-w-0">
			<div class="mirror-content">{{content}}</div>

			{{> "post/tags"}}

			{{> "post/share"}}

			{{> "post/end-blocks"}}
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
